# His father is alive.
{200}{}{Hi. Are you a wanderer? My dad says wanderers are trouble until they prove different. Have you proved different yet?}
{201}{}{Working on it. Who's your dad?}
{202}{}{What do you know about the bomb?}
{203}{}{You small. Me big.}
{204}{}{Stay out of trouble, kid.}
{205}{}{You're the one who fixed the bomb! Dad says you're all right. He doesn't say that about anybody. Not even me, much.}
{210}{}{Lucas Simms. He's the sheriff AND the mayor. He shot a raider once from clear across the crater. Mister Stockholm says it was luck, but Mister Stockholm wasn't even born.}
{215}{}{The church people say it's Atom. Dad says it's two tons of trouble. I threw a rock at it once. Don't tell.}
{216}{}{It doesn't tick any more. I listened. The church people are sad about it, but I think they like being sad.}
{220}{}{Yeah. But I've got a star.}
{221}{}{Star shiny.}

# His father is dead.
{230}{}{That man in the suit shot my dad. In the back. Dad always said watch their hands, and he did, and it didn't matter.}
{231}{}{My dad's dead. He was the sheriff and the mayor, and now he's just dead.}
{232}{}{Harden. The bomb is dead. I disarmed it.}
{233}{}{I'm sorry, Harden.}
{234}{}{Take care of yourself.}
{235}{}{Everybody's sorry. I've got his hat. It doesn't fit yet.}
{236}{}{Boom ball quiet now. Me fix.}
{237}{}{Me go.}
{240}{}{Dad said if anybody ever killed that bomb, the town pays three hundred dollars and they get the empty house by the gate. It's in his book. I counted the money twice. Here. And the key.}
{241}{}{Your father would be proud of you.}
{242}{}{Thank you, Sheriff.}
{243}{}{Thank you, small sheriff.}
{245}{}{I keep the book now. You're in it. On the good page.}
